  "id": "DrugBank_DB04897 - MONDO_9971",
  "verbalization": "Lucinactant is implicated in the pathogenesis of Newborn Respiratory Distress Syndrome (NRDS) through its association with Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS), a condition that is often linked to NRDS in preterm infants. The evidence suggests that Lucinactant may exert a protective or modulatory effect on the respiratory system, potentially mitigating the severity of ARDS and thereby reducing the risk of NRDS. This is supported by the shared indication of Lucinactant with other agents like Poractant Alfa and Colfosceril Palmitate, which are also used in the management of ARDS and are associated with NRDS. The integrated evidence implies that Lucinactant may act through mechanisms that influence pulmonary function or inflammation, thereby contributing to the prevention or alleviation of NRDS. The recurring association with ARDS suggests a potential role in the pathophysiology of NRDS, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
